WEEK 13 — REFUND METHOD AND DRAWER SAFETY

Date: Monday, 2 November 2026

Problem: A cash refund larger than the cash in the drawer would leave the drawer negative.

Solution:
- The cashier first sees a quote with the exact refund and note split.
- Cash refunds are checked against the cash in the drawer before anything is written.
- Card or UPI refunds go back to the original payment through the gateway.
- Points used on the returned part come back as points, not cash.
- The desk warns the cashier and asks them to switch the method or top up the drawer.
